WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.000
[ Watch on KissFlix.co ]

2
00:00.000 --> 00:01.000
MkvDrama.net

3
01:39.000 --> 01:42.674
(A few years ago, my father passed away from a chronic illness.)

4
01:44.470 --> 01:46.002
(He was 60 years old.)

5
01:47.191 --> 01:49.296
(I think he’s gone too soon.)

6
01:49.320 --> 01:50.248
MR. JIRA JAROENWONG BORN FEBRUARY 3, 1960, DIED APRIL 18, 2020

7
01:50.290 --> 01:52.300
(Why couldn’t he live to 70 or 80?)

8
02:06.653 --> 02:08.000
(But who would have thought…)

9
02:09.300 --> 02:11.798
(That my life would only be half as long as his.)

10
02:18.470 --> 02:19.669
(My dad’s gone.)

11
02:20.990 --> 02:23.697
(My sister got married and moved overseas with her husband.)

12
02:25.000 --> 02:26.300
(My mom went along with them.)

13
02:34.630 --> 02:35.400
(Friends?)

14
02:36.610 --> 02:37.565
(I have none.)

15
02:39.305 --> 02:40.200
(Lover?)

16
02:41.487 --> 02:42.730
(I don’t have that, either.)

17
02:53.951 --> 02:56.170
(Is that… the class president?)

18
02:57.980 --> 02:59.410
(If the person lying here were him…)

19
03:01.971 --> 03:04.247
(He’d have many things to think about before he died.)

20
03:05.635 --> 03:07.200
(In that final moment,)

21
03:09.460 --> 03:12.702
(I finally realized what I regretted most about my 30 years of life.)

22
03:16.019 --> 03:18.300
(I didn’t regret that no one remembered me.)

23
03:22.077 --> 03:25.297
(What I regretted was living my life without remembering anyone.)

24
03:44.746 --> 03:46.899
(Is this heaven or hell?)

25
03:48.490 --> 03:49.899
(Why does it feel like…)

26
03:51.654 --> 03:53.200
(I’m taking a nap at my old house?)

27
03:55.514 --> 03:56.299
Wait!

28
03:57.604 --> 03:58.800
My old house?

29
04:08.540 --> 04:09.760
Get up already.

30
04:10.214 --> 04:12.250
Stop making that confused face and mumbling.

31
04:18.829 --> 04:19.814
Where am I?

32
04:21.161 --> 04:23.198
You think you’re the main character in a novel?

33
04:23.770 --> 04:25.463
Scoot over. I'm sitting here.

34
04:29.807 --> 04:31.601
Why are you dressed like this?

35
04:32.450 --> 04:33.268
Ji!

36
04:34.294 --> 04:35.330
Watch your mouth.

37
04:35.760 --> 04:37.580
I carried you all the way home.

38
04:38.040 --> 04:39.697
You didn’t even say thank you.

39
04:40.400 --> 04:41.200
Carried?

40
04:41.887 --> 04:43.220
Why did you have to carry me?

41
04:44.515 --> 04:48.068
Wasn’t it you who wanted to go out to join the water fight

42
04:48.111 --> 04:50.208
then got heatstroke and passed out in the alley?

43
04:50.761 --> 04:52.804
You freaked those people out.

44
05:11.656 --> 05:13.597
Oh, I remember now.

45
05:15.176 --> 05:16.100
Remember what?

46
05:17.219 --> 05:20.601
(But wasn’t that… Songkran from years ago?)

47
05:22.602 --> 05:23.697
(Then why…)

48
05:24.614 --> 05:26.299
Are you alright?

49
05:27.150 --> 05:32.300
Did you hit your head and lose your memory?

50
05:35.785 --> 05:38.100
(Damn it. What the hell is going on?)

51
05:39.257 --> 05:41.000
(Am I dreaming?)

52
05:44.001 --> 05:44.700
Ouch!

53
05:44.943 --> 05:47.798
Did your dad tell you to pinch my leg?!

54
05:48.887 --> 05:50.897
Wait, we have the same dad.

55
05:51.910 --> 05:52.697
Oww.

56
05:55.939 --> 05:58.697
(That means… this is really not a dream?)

57
06:01.730 --> 06:02.497
Mhee!

58
06:05.838 --> 06:07.023
I miss you so much.

59
06:08.543 --> 06:09.801
I really miss you.

60
06:09.884 --> 06:11.900
What are you guys yelling about?

61
06:14.225 --> 06:15.002
Mom!

62
06:17.188 --> 06:19.400
Mom, this brat… He pinched me.

63
06:20.410 --> 06:22.684
How many times have I told you not to call him that?

64
06:22.820 --> 06:23.937
You, too, Ji.

65
06:24.248 --> 06:25.730
What did you do to your sister?

66
06:26.297 --> 06:27.900
I’m bruised, see?

67
06:30.402 --> 06:32.094
(2010.)

68
06:32.680 --> 06:33.980
(That means…)

69
06:38.630 --> 06:40.598
Mom called and told me you passed out.

70
06:41.573 --> 06:45.000
I told you to wait and go with us in the evening.

71
06:54.560 --> 06:57.450
MR. JIRAPHAT JAROENWONG BORN FEBRUARY 3, 1960, DIED APRIL 18, 2020

72
07:02.992 --> 07:03.696
Dad!

73
07:05.130 --> 07:06.699
Hey, wait, wait, wait.

74
07:07.884 --> 07:09.654
Why are you hugging me, huh?

75
07:13.697 --> 07:14.420
Hey.

76
07:15.035 --> 07:16.499
Are you crying?

77
07:17.780 --> 07:19.798
Did Jean pick on you?

78
07:20.130 --> 07:21.939
-I didn’t. This brat… -Watch it!

79
07:22.810 --> 07:25.102
Ji pinched me first.

80
07:26.782 --> 07:27.613
What is it?

81
07:29.595 --> 07:31.100
Okay, okay, okay.

82
07:52.920 --> 08:01.320
JIRA, NARUMON, JEAN

83
08:13.939 --> 08:17.400
AAH! What the hell is this?!

84
08:22.780 --> 08:23.703
A dream?

85
08:24.742 --> 08:26.897
If this is just a dream,

86
08:27.928 --> 08:29.690
I’ll wake up in my bed in my condo.

87
08:40.550 --> 08:41.801
It’s just a dream.

88
08:44.300 --> 08:46.601
It’s just a dream. That’s all.

89
08:49.416 --> 08:50.397
Go to sleep.

90
09:27.111 --> 09:29.601
(Ji, wake up!)

91
09:30.200 --> 09:32.404
(You’re gonna sleep in every day during school break?)

92
09:33.170 --> 09:34.354
Okay, I’m up.

93
09:34.558 --> 09:38.401
(Then come down for breakfast. Mom and Dad are waiting.)

94
09:38.524 --> 09:40.601
(I’m gonna be late for dorm check-in.)

95
09:40.640 --> 09:41.699
I heard you.

96
09:47.290 --> 09:51.000
Did I… really travel back in time?

97
09:57.312 --> 09:58.699
Ahh!

98
09:59.368 --> 10:01.737
-(Ji, get up!) -Fine!

99
10:04.331 --> 10:06.800
Finish your breakfast. I’m gonna be late.

100
10:06.977 --> 10:08.600
I’ll drive you there so fast.

101
10:10.270 --> 10:11.300
Eat a lot.

102
10:12.435 --> 10:13.650
There’s plenty of food.

103
10:13.840 --> 10:15.379
You’re not hungry?

104
10:15.675 --> 10:16.700
Don’t you like the food?

105
10:16.737 --> 10:17.702
I do.

106
10:21.645 --> 10:22.600
This is good.

107
10:25.188 --> 10:27.497
You need to eat plenty of healthy food, Dad.

108
10:29.230 --> 10:31.201
You should also cut back on alcohol and beer.

109
10:32.597 --> 10:34.481
Why are you so worried about me, hmm?

110
10:35.183 --> 10:36.601
Eat lots of protein.

111
10:38.321 --> 10:39.453
Such a suck-up.

112
10:40.663 --> 10:42.065
Eat a lot.

113
10:42.470 --> 10:43.300
Yes, Mom.

114
10:46.450 --> 10:47.970
Jean, you didn’t forget anything, did you?

115
10:48.010 --> 10:49.099
No, Mom.

116
10:49.430 --> 10:51.601
But if I did, I can come back and get it later.

117
10:52.050 --> 10:54.398
Call me when you get to the dorm, okay?

118
10:54.505 --> 10:56.770
Eh? You’re not coming with me?

119
10:58.551 --> 11:00.420
I have to make desserts for my customers.

120
11:00.460 --> 11:01.700
I really can’t go.

121
11:02.125 --> 11:03.977
But it’s three months.

122
11:04.080 --> 11:04.979
Oh, please.

123
11:05.130 --> 11:07.210
You’re a senior. Don’t act like a child.

124
11:07.948 --> 11:08.457
You brat.

125
11:08.690 --> 11:09.899
“You brat. You brat”

126
11:10.168 --> 11:12.804
-I told you not to call him that. -Right.

127
11:13.210 --> 11:15.204
And you, stop messing with your sister.

128
11:15.238 --> 11:18.102
When she’s gone, you’re gonna be lonely.

129
11:19.016 --> 11:19.700
I won’t.

130
11:21.460 --> 11:23.045
Drive safely, honey.

131
11:23.540 --> 11:24.545
I know, honey.

132
11:25.142 --> 11:26.099
Come on, Jean.

133
11:27.100 --> 11:29.197
-Give me a hug. -Bye-bye, Mom.

134
11:30.250 --> 11:31.598
See you, Mom.

135
11:31.800 --> 11:32.896
Give me a hug.

136
11:34.920 --> 11:35.897
-Bye-bye. -Let’s go.

137
11:36.690 --> 11:37.745
My hair’s messed up.

138
11:41.040 --> 11:41.899
Bye.

139
11:43.785 --> 11:45.392
Come help me make the desserts.

140
11:45.428 --> 11:46.297
Okay, Mom.

141
11:57.360 --> 11:58.602
I broke it again.

142
11:58.942 --> 12:02.059
Thai desserts take lots of patience to make.

143
12:02.829 --> 12:04.400
I’m trying to be patient.

144
12:06.068 --> 12:07.397
Go find something to do.

145
12:07.760 --> 12:08.997
I can do this myself.

146
12:10.420 --> 12:11.899
But I want to help you.

147
12:12.213 --> 12:15.580
But I think I can do it faster by myself.

148
12:15.746 --> 12:16.496
Mom.

149
12:18.060 --> 12:20.457
It’s your school break. I want you to relax.

150
12:20.780 --> 12:22.275
If you don’t know where to go,

151
12:22.324 --> 12:25.250
grab the money on the TV and go get some ice-cream.

152
12:26.630 --> 12:28.703
I’m not a kid. I don’t eat ice-cream.

153
12:29.480 --> 12:30.302
Hmm?

154
12:35.001 --> 12:35.697
Oh.

155
12:42.520 --> 12:47.290
NARONGRIT BOXING GYM

156
13:01.170 --> 13:02.337
I’ve read this already.

157
13:11.190 --> 13:13.111
I’ve read this, too.

158
13:20.731 --> 13:22.700
Isn’t there something new, Chok?

159
13:23.670 --> 13:26.002
But the one in your hand’s just arrived today, Ji.

160
13:38.620 --> 13:40.000
(He’s a generous man.)

161
13:40.810 --> 13:42.800
Ms. Orn still looks beautiful.

162
14:00.720 --> 14:03.699
The school is about to start. Why don’t you go out with your friends?

163
14:04.270 --> 14:06.802
Don’t you get bored being at home all the time?

164
14:08.678 --> 14:09.700
I don’t, Mom.

165
14:11.050 --> 14:13.200
I love having you at home

166
14:13.487 --> 14:16.001
but I want you to go out like other kids sometimes.

167
14:17.367 --> 14:21.099
In case one day your dad, Jean, and I are gone.

168
14:21.884 --> 14:24.139
I don’t want you to cry all by yourself.

169
14:24.183 --> 14:25.200
Do you understand?

170
14:57.616 --> 15:00.334
(To have other things to think about when I die,)

171
15:01.030 --> 15:03.270
(this Jiraphat will become a new person.)

172
15:13.300 --> 15:14.337
This year…

173
15:15.802 --> 15:17.777
2010.

174
15:19.128 --> 15:22.779
Until the day I died…

175
15:32.604 --> 15:33.998
2023.

176
15:37.057 --> 15:38.397
That means

177
15:44.616 --> 15:46.219
I have…

178
15:47.238 --> 15:49.899
13 years left to start over.

179
16:09.914 --> 16:11.697
If you run to school, you can get there in time, right?

180
16:12.160 --> 16:14.299
Your school is just around the corner.

181
16:18.103 --> 16:20.000
I don’t mind if you’re late.

182
16:20.528 --> 16:22.562
But you got up so early today.

183
16:22.600 --> 16:24.665
Do you want to arrive late anyway?

184
16:26.630 --> 16:27.468
Huh, Ji?

185
16:28.817 --> 16:30.539
See you then, Dad.

186
16:30.810 --> 16:31.598
Yeah.

187
16:32.644 --> 16:34.197
(This might seem silly.)

188
16:34.585 --> 16:36.977
(Will going to school early change anything?)

189
16:38.285 --> 16:40.299
(But for me who hadn’t made any progress)

190
16:40.680 --> 16:43.000
(from when my dad passed to the day I died,)

191
16:43.960 --> 16:46.142
(running forward as fast as I can,)

192
16:46.394 --> 16:47.210
Run, Ji, run!

193
16:49.127 --> 16:50.900
(It’s not just about getting to school in time.)

194
16:53.260 --> 16:57.398
(It’s my very first step to move forward from my meaningless life.)

195
17:14.186 --> 17:15.100
Yes!

196
17:18.040 --> 17:22.020
NAWINA SCHOOL

197
17:23.268 --> 17:24.020
Yes!

198
17:31.045 --> 17:35.660
♪ Thailand unites Thai people with flesh and blood. ♪

199
18:37.960 --> 18:41.200
PHAPPIM, LAWYER, IS NOT WORRIED THAT THE OPPOSING PARTY IS INFLUENTIAL.

200
18:41.240 --> 18:43.290
“UNDUE INFLUENCE CANNOT OVERRIDE THE LAW.”

201
18:43.330 --> 18:44.302
Jiraphat.

202
18:46.610 --> 18:48.202
Did you run away from the teachers?

203
18:50.262 --> 18:52.500
-No, I didn’t… -What are you doing?

204
18:54.025 --> 18:56.302
Hey, Ji. You’re not late, today?

205
18:56.608 --> 18:58.500
It’s the first day of school so I’m here early.

206
18:58.650 --> 19:01.776
But last semester, you were late since the first day.

207
19:01.810 --> 19:02.600
Mmm.

208
19:03.210 --> 19:05.696
Well, this semester is different because…

209
19:06.770 --> 19:07.800
-Because? -Because?

210
19:11.035 --> 19:13.093
Because I’m gonna be a good boy this semester!

211
19:20.801 --> 19:22.397
Don’t laugh at him.

212
19:22.909 --> 19:24.604
No, I’m not.

213
19:26.750 --> 19:27.650
Sorry, sorry.

214
19:27.943 --> 19:31.000
It’s just you talk like my nephew who’s in kindergarten.

215
19:31.700 --> 19:34.401
And you made a funny face.

216
19:35.485 --> 19:37.020
I couldn’t help but laugh a little.

217
19:37.394 --> 19:38.302
A little?

218
19:40.270 --> 19:43.270
But you seemed confident when you said that.

219
19:43.309 --> 19:46.182
I’ll believe you didn’t come to school late.

220
19:48.128 --> 19:50.800
Here’s the list of students in Grade 11, Class 7, Miss Prefect.

221
19:51.062 --> 19:52.100
Got it.

222
19:53.020 --> 19:54.696
I’ll go to the restroom now.

223
19:56.430 --> 19:58.980
Now that you’re here in time, don’t cut classes again.

224
20:02.515 --> 20:05.656
Hey, I’m sorry I laughed at you.

225
20:06.084 --> 20:07.192
And don’t worry.

226
20:07.226 --> 20:10.170
What you said earlier, I won’t tell anyone.

227
20:12.330 --> 20:13.401
See you in class.

228
20:25.170 --> 20:25.888
Look.

229
20:25.924 --> 20:27.737
Jiraphat, The Good Boy’s here, everyone.

230
20:27.820 --> 20:29.102
A round of applause.

231
20:29.394 --> 20:31.020
Woohoo!

232
20:35.520 --> 20:37.090
MONDAY, MAY 17

233
20:40.528 --> 20:41.797
Listen up, guys.

234
20:42.350 --> 20:45.734
I have news on Jiraphat, The Good Boy.

235
20:45.961 --> 20:46.700
Huh?

236
20:47.090 --> 20:49.302
Jiraphat, The Good Boy.

237
20:50.583 --> 20:51.505
What?

238
20:52.670 --> 20:53.798
Welcome, The Good Boy.

239
20:56.920 --> 20:57.800
Hi, Ji!

240
21:06.770 --> 21:07.531
Hi.

241
21:11.760 --> 21:12.980
How was your school break?

242
21:13.370 --> 21:14.802
It was good. You?

243
21:17.100 --> 21:17.951
I had so much fun.

244
21:17.990 --> 21:19.899
This year, my dad took me on a Songkran trip.

245
21:20.244 --> 21:22.862
We went to Silom, Khaosan, and around our house.

246
21:22.921 --> 21:25.382
They even put ice in the water they used.

247
21:25.557 --> 21:28.616
(I had a nice friend who sat next to me in class.)

248
21:32.303 --> 21:35.201
(But when I died, why didn’t I think of him?)

249
21:35.377 --> 21:36.302
(Hi, Ji!)

250
21:38.377 --> 21:39.099
Hi, Ji!

251
21:39.435 --> 21:40.200
Mmm.

252
21:41.120 --> 21:42.401
How was your school break?

253
21:42.970 --> 21:43.897
It was fine.

254
21:52.872 --> 21:54.602
Hey, Ked. Hey, Pim.

255
21:55.570 --> 21:56.404
Yeah?

256
21:57.220 --> 21:59.696
After the mid-term exam, I’m moving to England.

257
22:00.740 --> 22:02.397
I won’t see you guys anymore.

258
22:03.213 --> 22:04.499
Why move there so suddenly?

259
22:04.998 --> 22:07.640
My dad has to move for work quite often.

260
22:07.680 --> 22:09.299
So we have to move with him.

261
22:09.484 --> 22:10.600
But I’m used to it now.

262
22:11.120 --> 22:12.974
You two are going to miss me.

263
22:15.345 --> 22:17.097
Wanna go together next year?

264
22:23.008 --> 22:23.801
What?

265
22:25.540 --> 22:27.300
You want to hang out with me?

266
22:29.531 --> 22:31.582
I’m gonna cry right now.

267
22:35.120 --> 22:37.100
Let’s plan our Songkran trip for next year, Ji.

268
22:39.631 --> 22:41.217
Attention, students.

269
22:42.402 --> 22:44.340
All Good morning.

270
22:44.774 --> 22:46.100
Good morning, everyone.

271
22:46.440 --> 22:48.460
We’ve met before in social studies class.

272
22:48.786 --> 22:50.930
But today, I’d like to introduce myself again.

273
22:51.130 --> 22:52.401
I’m Mr. Tinnapob.

274
22:52.440 --> 22:53.413
You can call me Mr. Tin.

275
22:53.450 --> 22:56.700
I’ll be your homeroom teacher for Grade 11, Class 7, this academic year.

276
22:56.925 --> 22:57.902
Nice to see you all.

277
23:16.770 --> 23:18.300
Please, I have to get to class.

278
23:18.600 --> 23:19.798
What’s the problem?!

279
23:27.121 --> 23:27.903
Why so scared?

280
23:28.054 --> 23:29.220
-Hey, you. -Come on, try this.

281
23:29.574 --> 23:30.600
We’re at school.

282
23:35.950 --> 23:37.001
None of your business!

283
23:42.890 --> 23:43.702
Jiraphat.

284
23:44.800 --> 23:46.287
Jiraphat, The Good Boy, right?

285
23:46.534 --> 23:48.062
You can’t smoke in school.

286
23:48.100 --> 23:48.715
Why not?

287
23:48.760 --> 23:51.008
Jiraphat, The Good Boy is worried about my health?

288
23:51.047 --> 23:53.340
You can smoke 100 cigarettes a day if you want.

289
23:53.379 --> 23:54.700
I don’t even care.

290
23:55.042 --> 23:56.410
But I just want to warn you.

291
23:56.607 --> 23:59.080
If you keep smoking like this, you’re gonna die someday.

292
23:59.108 --> 24:00.598
But not from lung cancer.

293
24:00.669 --> 24:02.960
But from smoking where you shouldn’t.

294
24:03.070 --> 24:04.001
You jackass!

295
24:05.190 --> 24:06.097
Kongpob!

296
24:06.310 --> 24:07.200
Jiraphat!

297
24:13.205 --> 24:15.450
I was told you guys were smoking.

298
24:17.447 --> 24:18.462
-I… -Go!

299
24:19.770 --> 24:21.598
Go to the disciplinary office now.

300
24:24.508 --> 24:25.400
Excuse me.

301
24:33.674 --> 24:35.002
I was in the toilet.

302
24:35.776 --> 24:37.202
Jiraphat wasn’t smoking.

303
24:39.881 --> 24:41.201
I think you’re misinformed.

304
24:44.580 --> 24:46.100
I got it, Atiwitch.

305
24:46.390 --> 24:47.749
You get to class.

306
24:48.841 --> 24:52.337
Jiraphat, you go to the disciplinary office.

307
24:53.632 --> 24:54.700
-But, sir. -But, sir.

308
24:55.574 --> 24:56.802
What’s wrong with you guys?

309
24:57.270 --> 24:58.502
You think I don’t know.

310
24:58.840 --> 25:01.097
Jiraphat is always late to school.

311
25:01.810 --> 25:06.180
But when school’s over, he’s always the first to run out.

312
25:07.180 --> 25:10.364
Do you think this guy will get himself in trouble

313
25:10.400 --> 25:11.897
and get detention after school?

314
25:12.010 --> 25:13.826
You smell like smoke.

315
25:13.870 --> 25:15.520
How can I let you go to class like this?

316
25:15.840 --> 25:18.401
Go spray some air freshener in my office.

317
25:19.454 --> 25:20.370
And you, Kongpob,

318
25:21.432 --> 25:22.920
We have to talk.

319
25:23.035 --> 25:23.894
Come with me!

320
25:57.768 --> 26:00.297
Jiraphat, go to class.

321
26:00.530 --> 26:01.260
Yes, sir.

322
26:04.980 --> 26:05.998
Go.

323
26:06.470 --> 26:08.598
You want to be punished with Kongpob or what?

324
26:09.078 --> 26:10.536
No, sir. Thank you, sir.

325
26:23.188 --> 26:23.850
Hey, Ji!

326
26:24.565 --> 26:25.462
Are you alright?

327
26:25.939 --> 26:26.860
Are you hurt?

328
26:27.865 --> 26:29.100
What do you mean?

329
26:29.656 --> 26:32.260
I heard you got into a fight with Kongpob from class 9.

330
26:32.693 --> 26:34.097
You have to be careful.

331
26:34.380 --> 26:37.500
Last semester, whenever I ran into him, I came back with bruises.

332
26:38.308 --> 26:39.750
It was just a misunderstanding.

333
26:39.789 --> 26:41.330
Not that big of a deal.

334
26:42.402 --> 26:44.023
How did you hear about this anyway?

335
26:44.274 --> 26:45.773
Oh, from her.

336
26:49.230 --> 26:51.899
Hey, I heard it from Lita.

337
26:52.411 --> 26:53.602
Haven’t you heard?

338
26:54.038 --> 26:55.100
What Lita knows…

339
26:55.480 --> 26:57.090
-The world knows. -The world knows.

340
26:58.811 --> 27:00.185
It’s good that you’re okay.

341
27:00.990 --> 27:02.847
You’re so tiny.

342
27:03.408 --> 27:05.100
Next time, I’m gonna deal with him.

343
27:08.223 --> 27:11.256
What are you making so much noise? I could hear you from outside.

344
27:15.640 --> 27:19.044
Can’t you just behave and be responsible, like those in the science class?

345
27:20.050 --> 27:21.847
You guys are killing me.

346
27:23.546 --> 27:25.401
Now, don’t just sit there.

347
27:25.890 --> 27:27.059
Bring out your textbook!

348
27:37.546 --> 27:39.616
Attention, students.

349
27:40.257 --> 27:42.601
Thank you, ma’am.

350
27:45.174 --> 27:46.398
Ji, are you okay?

351
27:47.059 --> 27:47.798
Yeah.

352
27:48.170 --> 27:49.398
But class is dismissed.

353
27:50.350 --> 27:52.001
And what?

354
27:52.395 --> 27:55.690
Normally, when the bell rings, you run out of the classroom.

355
27:55.725 --> 27:57.520
You don’t even wait for the teacher to leave.

356
27:58.682 --> 28:00.736
What do you usually do after school?

357
28:01.590 --> 28:03.414
I used to play sports with other people,

358
28:03.700 --> 28:05.970
but I think they didn’t like that I was taller than them.

359
28:06.014 --> 28:09.216
So I’d get something delicious to eat before taking the bus home,

360
28:09.251 --> 28:11.004
then play badminton with my dad.

361
28:12.327 --> 28:13.802
Hold on.

362
28:14.712 --> 28:16.801
You’re asking because…

363
28:18.739 --> 28:19.897
Great, Ji!

364
28:19.982 --> 28:21.579
Wanna have frozen egg yolk ice-cream?

365
28:21.838 --> 28:24.734
-Why not? -Let’s go. What are we waiting for?

366
28:26.890 --> 28:28.967
There are lots of good treats around our school.

367
28:29.010 --> 28:30.700
Today we had frozen egg yolk ice-cream, right?

368
28:30.736 --> 28:32.620
Should we have rolled pancakes tomorrow?

369
28:32.656 --> 28:34.220
Let’s try everything around here?

370
29:16.750 --> 29:18.797
Umm, can I ask you something?

371
29:19.422 --> 29:20.299
Yes, Ji.

372
29:20.554 --> 29:22.417
You’re two years younger than us, right?

373
29:22.800 --> 29:23.897
That’s right.

374
29:24.620 --> 29:26.710
Then why am I the only one you consider your senior?

375
29:26.750 --> 29:28.302
You don’t do the same with the others.

376
29:28.717 --> 29:31.065
Oh, I do, actually.

377
29:31.100 --> 29:33.300
But some of them think that makes them look old.

378
29:33.390 --> 29:35.337
And some think I’m messing with them.

379
29:35.591 --> 29:38.820
You’re the only one who doesn’t have a problem with that.

380
29:39.920 --> 29:41.770
NAWINA SCHOOL

381
29:45.910 --> 29:47.000
What are you doing?

382
29:47.230 --> 29:49.822
Is that Kongpob, the guy who picked on you?

383
29:51.720 --> 29:52.819
Don’t be afraid, Ji.

384
29:53.230 --> 29:55.296
Stay behind me. I’ll take care of this.

385
29:58.447 --> 30:00.480
Hey! Mr. Kongpob.

386
30:01.705 --> 30:02.543
What’s your problem?

387
30:03.320 --> 30:07.402
I heard you were picking on my best friend, Ji.

388
30:10.925 --> 30:11.582
So?

389
30:14.850 --> 30:15.751
You see this?

390
30:18.456 --> 30:19.650
Do you know what it is?

391
30:19.690 --> 30:20.598
What is it?

392
30:21.005 --> 30:22.398
-The Man-eating Bush! -Hey!

393
30:23.930 --> 30:25.253
Ha! How was that?

394
30:25.290 --> 30:26.465
That’s for messing with my best friend.

395
30:27.351 --> 30:28.201
Ty!

396
30:28.235 --> 30:29.097
Assh*le!

397
30:29.540 --> 30:30.302
Hey!

398
30:30.520 --> 30:31.297
Stop it!

399
30:32.080 --> 30:33.145
What’s going on now?!

400
30:39.506 --> 30:41.800
You already caused problems during lunch break.

401
30:42.640 --> 30:43.997
Wasn’t that enough?

402
30:45.010 --> 30:46.000
Jiraphat.

403
30:46.540 --> 30:47.598
Kongpob.

404
30:48.771 --> 30:49.700
And this time,

405
30:50.430 --> 30:51.600
Tyler, too.

406
30:53.589 --> 30:55.500
What were you doing in the bush?

407
30:55.737 --> 30:57.297
I think you’re misunderstanding.

408
30:57.340 --> 30:58.598
Misunderstanding?

409
30:59.950 --> 31:03.602
The same two boys who were having a fight during lunch break.

410
31:04.066 --> 31:06.500
One of them was lying in the bush, cursing.

411
31:06.800 --> 31:08.290
And the other was standing there laughing.

412
31:09.334 --> 31:12.540
Was that how you guys made up, huh?

413
31:12.880 --> 31:14.011
-Well… -Sir!

414
31:14.974 --> 31:16.204
Let me explain.

415
31:16.903 --> 31:17.780
Ji, don’t worry.

416
31:18.167 --> 31:19.777
Just stand there.

417
31:19.943 --> 31:22.090
You’ll get to have egg yolk ice-cream in no time.

418
31:23.697 --> 31:26.001
Well, here’s what happened.

419
31:26.718 --> 31:29.577
Have you ever heard about this myth?

420
31:30.340 --> 31:32.820
It’s called The Man-eating Bush.

421
31:51.875 --> 31:55.183
Tyler, this is what you call having egg yolk ice-cream?

422
31:56.702 --> 31:57.982
It wasn’t my fault, Ji.

423
31:58.379 --> 31:59.600
It was Mr. Narong’s.

424
31:59.908 --> 32:01.896
He just doesn’t get us teenagers.

425
32:02.182 --> 32:04.880
If you hadn’t said all that stuff, this would have been over.

426
32:04.910 --> 32:07.499
I wasn’t trying to be funny, I was serious.

427
32:08.032 --> 32:08.900
It’s Mr. Narong.

428
32:08.940 --> 32:10.900
I thought he liked students who are honest.

429
32:14.364 --> 32:15.140
Tyler!

430
32:17.350 --> 32:20.099
The Man-eating Bush.

431
32:34.970 --> 32:35.699
Hey, Kong.

432
32:35.740 --> 32:37.531
I didn’t know you wanted to be in The Man-eating Bush.

433
32:37.571 --> 32:38.930
You caught me off guard.

434
32:39.013 --> 32:40.010
Are you okay?

435
32:40.979 --> 32:42.402
-The Man-eating Bush! -Oww!

436
32:44.550 --> 32:45.400
Kong.

437
32:46.630 --> 32:48.202
You guys, look this way.

438
32:48.308 --> 32:49.398
-Ouch. -Ouch.

439
32:49.814 --> 32:51.136
You both look so funny.

440
32:56.361 --> 32:57.798
Smile. Yeah, yeah, like that.

441
32:58.041 --> 32:58.982
Smile, smile, smile.

442
33:00.296 --> 33:01.299
Yeah.

443
33:01.899 --> 33:02.800
Having fun?

444
33:02.840 --> 33:03.897
So much fun!

445
33:13.868 --> 33:15.659
What are you doing here, sir?

446
33:16.293 --> 33:17.580
Wanna see these pictures?

447
33:19.810 --> 33:22.223
-I’ll pick up the trash over there then! -Tyler, stop!

448
33:22.373 --> 33:23.099
Tyler!

449
33:23.880 --> 33:25.540
Tyler, stop!

450
33:26.160 --> 33:28.520
ATIWITCH RATTANAWATTHANA, CLASS PRESIDENT

451
33:32.090 --> 33:34.400
You guys, I have some news.

452
33:35.625 --> 33:37.900
I was at the disciplinary office

453
33:37.940 --> 33:39.971
and saw Mr. Narong questioning some students.

454
33:40.008 --> 33:41.214
I think I saw…

455
33:41.240 --> 33:42.620
Jiraphat, The Good Boy

456
33:43.260 --> 33:45.897
and Kongpob from class 9, who was caught smoking.

457
33:46.170 --> 33:48.700
And the other one was Tyler.

458
33:49.035 --> 33:50.177
And what happened?

459
33:50.550 --> 33:52.296
It was nothing serious.

460
33:52.340 --> 33:54.860
Mr. Narong just misunderstood something.

461
33:55.351 --> 33:56.900
What was it about this time?

462
33:57.817 --> 33:59.002
The Man-eating Bush.

463
33:59.517 --> 34:00.139
Huh?

464
34:00.400 --> 34:03.010
Yeah. Even Mr. Narong was stunned.

465
34:04.866 --> 34:07.400
What’s The Man-eating Bush?

466
34:08.920 --> 34:10.499
How long have you been here?

467
34:10.540 --> 34:12.720
Haven’t you heard about The Man-eating Bush?

468
34:12.893 --> 34:17.416
If you really want to know, why don’t you ask Tyler or Jiraphat?

469
34:17.503 --> 34:18.060
Mmm.

470
34:23.482 --> 34:24.401
I’m home.

471
34:24.982 --> 34:25.997
Good evening.

472
34:26.914 --> 34:28.360
You came home late today.

473
34:28.398 --> 34:30.000
Dinner is all cold.

474
34:30.330 --> 34:32.314
I’ll go heat it up. Wait a minute.

475
34:32.349 --> 34:33.699
Oh, it’s okay, Mom.

476
34:33.924 --> 34:35.303
I forgot to call you.

477
34:42.185 --> 34:44.577
How was your first day of the semester?

478
34:45.805 --> 34:46.702
Well…

479
34:48.540 --> 34:49.602
It was fun.

480
34:58.688 --> 35:01.023
If you don’t have anything to do, let’s just go home.

481
35:03.370 --> 35:04.899
What are you guys doing here?

482
35:05.472 --> 35:06.970
Oh, hey, Lita.

483
35:07.457 --> 35:09.814
Don’t you have work to do?

484
35:09.968 --> 35:11.383
Ty, don’t be rude.

485
35:12.057 --> 35:14.297
I’ve already done my part.

486
35:14.870 --> 35:15.622
Mmm…

487
35:15.920 --> 35:20.198
If you guys are free, do you want to play volleyball with us?

488
35:34.625 --> 35:35.930
Ty, don’t use your feet.

489
35:35.970 --> 35:37.190
Why not?

490
35:37.232 --> 35:40.130
I saw it on TV. Those athletes all use their feet.

491
35:40.216 --> 35:43.030
That’s for getting the ball up or catching it in an emergency.

492
35:43.360 --> 35:45.653
Who uses their feet all the time like you?

493
35:47.902 --> 35:49.502
Ji, catch this.

494
35:56.125 --> 35:57.200
Wow, Ji!

495
36:08.820 --> 36:10.302
Sh*t!

496
36:12.540 --> 36:13.757
Are you okay, President?

497
36:13.800 --> 36:14.601
President!

498
36:15.188 --> 36:17.625
Ji, take him to the medical room now!

499
36:35.168 --> 36:36.497
Don’t worry, Jiraphat.

500
36:36.970 --> 36:38.296
Ruth will be just fine.

501
36:39.080 --> 36:40.598
But he’s unconscious right now.

502
36:40.816 --> 36:43.057
Oh, he’s just sleeping.

503
36:44.400 --> 36:45.299
Sleeping?

504
36:45.792 --> 36:47.502
Yes, look.

505
36:48.075 --> 36:49.422
He’s sleeping like a child.

506
36:53.302 --> 36:56.690
I told him to get some rest and not to work too hard.

507
36:57.330 --> 36:59.177
He’s the class president

508
36:59.222 --> 37:01.400
and he also has extra classes after school.

509
37:02.197 --> 37:03.776
He’ll probably wake up soon.

510
37:40.017 --> 37:40.660
Ji.

511
37:45.068 --> 37:45.819
Jiraphat?

512
37:53.758 --> 37:56.300
Oh, I’m the one who took you here.

513
37:56.869 --> 37:59.903
The teacher asked me to tell you to get some rest.

514
38:06.020 --> 38:07.700
-Get some rest? -Yes.

515
38:08.210 --> 38:10.677
You’ve been working too hard. You need to rest.

516
38:11.140 --> 38:13.001
You’re doing everything.

517
38:13.090 --> 38:14.400
Don’t you ever get tired?

518
38:26.130 --> 38:28.195
Why are you staring at me like that?

519
38:29.257 --> 38:30.659
Are you hurt anywhere?

520
38:30.699 --> 38:32.137
Do you want me to go get the teacher?

521
38:34.160 --> 38:35.065
I’m okay.

522
38:42.330 --> 38:44.202
No one’s said that to me in a long time.

523
38:56.550 --> 38:57.800
No one, huh?

524
38:58.708 --> 39:00.097
Give me some credit.

525
39:00.800 --> 39:03.653
I was just asking you during lunch break.

526
39:03.860 --> 39:05.945
“Are you tired?” “Wanna take a break?”

527
39:06.659 --> 39:10.342
Now Ji will think the student council’s making you work too hard.

528
39:12.940 --> 39:14.604
Where’s Tyler?

529
39:15.445 --> 39:18.020
Oh, Tyler’s not coming.

530
39:25.790 --> 39:29.115
(Will you take these documents and put them on Mr. Narong’s desk?)

531
39:29.157 --> 39:31.300
(I’ll go up to get the president’s bag.)

532
39:31.592 --> 39:33.600
(And I’ll see you at the medical room.)

533
40:11.219 --> 40:12.099
Ji’s here!

534
40:12.445 --> 40:14.337
Come on, come on. Help me take a look.

535
40:15.717 --> 40:16.503
Kongpob,

536
40:17.041 --> 40:18.401
what are you doing here?

537
40:18.677 --> 40:19.539
Ask your friend.

538
40:19.872 --> 40:21.862
Oh, please, Kong.

539
40:22.120 --> 40:23.623
We were in The Man-eatng Bush together.

540
40:23.656 --> 40:25.600
That means we’re friends now!

541
40:29.000 --> 40:29.900
Here’s what happened, Ji.

542
40:30.290 --> 40:33.550
While Mr. Narong was yelling at me for getting these answer sheets wet,

543
40:33.590 --> 40:34.730
Kong walked in.

544
40:35.665 --> 40:37.863
And he was kind enough to help me.

545
40:37.982 --> 40:40.509
Please. I just wanted you to shut up.

546
40:40.549 --> 40:41.374
Kong, my friend.

547
40:41.470 --> 40:44.770
We don’t use that kind of language anymore.

548
40:50.340 --> 40:51.197
Ji.

549
40:52.672 --> 40:55.222
Do you think this is number 2?

550
40:58.137 --> 40:59.296
I think it’s 8.

551
40:59.511 --> 41:00.419
You misunderstood.

552
41:00.580 --> 41:02.201
That’s obviously 0.

553
41:02.373 --> 41:03.340
Are you two blind?

554
41:04.466 --> 41:05.302
Oh.

555
41:05.644 --> 41:07.200
You’re so mean, Kong.

556
41:07.380 --> 41:11.622
Should we just give them the full scores? Mr. Narong would never know.

557
41:11.862 --> 41:13.980
Write 0 so they’ll have to come see Mr. Narong every day.

558
41:14.291 --> 41:15.665
I’d feel so sorry for this kid.

559
41:16.546 --> 41:18.303
I think I should write 100.

560
41:18.367 --> 41:19.216
0.

561
41:19.597 --> 41:20.660
-100. -0.

562
41:20.685 --> 41:21.342
-100. -0.

563
41:21.350 --> 41:22.146
Hey, hey, hey.

564
41:22.660 --> 41:24.577
I think 50 is perfect. Meet in the middle.

565
41:25.210 --> 41:26.000
49.

566
41:26.725 --> 41:27.659
-No! -49!

567
41:27.699 --> 41:28.349
-50! -100!

568
41:28.382 --> 41:29.337
-49! -100!

569
41:29.370 --> 41:30.816
-49! -In the middle!

570
41:30.850 --> 41:31.524
-49!

571
41:31.552 --> 41:32.099
100!

572
41:32.130 --> 41:32.921
Hey, 49!

573
41:32.945 --> 41:33.909
-50! -49!

574
41:33.930 --> 41:35.568
Hey, I’ll write 100!

575
41:37.512 --> 41:41.965
Tawan wanted me to tell you that all documents were taken care of.

576
41:42.010 --> 41:44.000
You can go home. See you tomorrow.

577
41:45.607 --> 41:46.300
Wait.

578
41:47.127 --> 41:47.900
What?

579
41:49.570 --> 41:51.499
What date and year is it?

580
41:53.511 --> 41:55.001
Why are you asking?

581
41:58.694 --> 42:01.097
May 31, 2010.

582
42:02.358 --> 42:03.195
See you.

583
42:08.970 --> 42:10.152
Why don’t you go today?

584
42:10.641 --> 42:12.600
Because I have no money left.

585
43:05.720 --> 43:07.360
What is everyone freaking out about?

586
43:07.400 --> 43:09.500
It’s Ms. Suda’s homework, of course.

587
43:09.635 --> 43:10.434
I finished it.

588
43:10.484 --> 43:11.250
Huh?

589
43:12.029 --> 43:13.560
Can I sit here?

590
43:14.360 --> 43:15.303
Scoot over.

591
43:16.850 --> 43:18.004
Hey, hey, hey.

592
43:19.640 --> 43:20.807
Tawan!

593
43:20.850 --> 43:22.737
I only had two pieces.

594
43:22.780 --> 43:24.820
Since you threw the volleyball in his face,

595
43:25.899 --> 43:28.080
you seem to be interested in him.

596
43:28.080 --> 43:29.080
MkvDrama.net
